IV. Merge Sort
Definition: Merge Sort is a divide-and-conquer sorting algorithm that divides an array into smaller subarrays,
recursively sorts them, and then merges the sorted subarrays to produce a sorted array.

Time Complexity: Best Case: O (n log n)
			   Worst Case: O (n log n)
Space Complexity: O (n)

Conclusion: Merge Sort is an efficient, stable, and predictable sorting algorithm with O(n log n) time complexity in the best, average,
and worst cases. However, it requires O(n) extra space, making it less memory-efficient than some in-place algorithms.

